<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adam Kok III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1811">1811</a>–<a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adam Kok III was kaptein of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippolis">Philippolis</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> from 1837. He sought British protection against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> settlers, but after the creation of the Orange Free State his people lost much of their land. In the early 1860s he led them over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a> to a new territory, Griqualand East, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokstad">Kokstad</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed in 1874.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adam-kok-iii.jpg" alt="Adam Kok III" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NtandoPZ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adam_Kok_III_bust.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
